## Gadget and Equipment System

- A dedicated Gadget Wheel has been added.
- The Gadget Wheel can be opened by hovering your right hand over your left and selecting an option with the right hand.
- Tapping the equipment input switches between primary webs and the selected secondary gadget.
- Players can choose and save their own gadget loadout.
- Gadgets can remain active while switching back to standard webs when supported.
- Gadget ammunition and ability energy use dedicated recharge systems.
- Players can choose whether abilities activate from the head button or through the alternate movement input.

### Web Bullets

- Web Bullets now use target seeking.
- Hits to an enemy’s head can deal damage.
- Shots to an injured enemy’s legs can trip and ragdoll them.
- Shots to the arms or torso can wrap eligible enemies.
- Riot enemies must generally be attacked from behind to be wrapped.
- Web Bullets can push physical objects.
- Repeated shots can detonate explosive barrels.

### Sonic Blaster

- The Sonic Blaster fires a forceful blast from either hand.
- Blasts can throw enemies backward.
- The recoil can be used for locomotion and additional aerial jumps.

### Web Shield

- The Web Shield protects the player from incoming damage and degrades as it absorbs hits.
- The shield can remain active while switching back to standard webs.
- Players can target an enemy with the shield hand and temporarily store that lock.
- The shield can then be thrown toward the stored target.
- A thrown shield can bounce from the target and return to the player.
- The shield remains usable while swinging.
- Shield attacks increase physical impact force without directly increasing punch damage.
- Shield damage and destruction are communicated through dedicated visual and audio effects.

### Web Fists

- Web Fists greatly increase the knockback force of punches.
- Each hand can deliver up to eight enhanced strikes.
- Web Fists can remain active while the player switches back to standard webs.
- Picking up an object temporarily disables the fist on that hand until the object is released.

### Web Bow

- The Web Bow fires fast, long-range web arrows.
- Arrows can penetrate enemies.
- Each arrow deals 33 damage.
- Headshots deal 66 damage.
- Arrows use target tracking.
- Each bow provides eight arrows before consuming its equipment charge.
- Bow arrows can detonate grenades and rockets.
- Players can return to standard tethering while the bow remains active.

### Web Staff

- The Web Staff provides a dedicated melee weapon.
- Spinning staff attacks deal 15 damage per hit.
- Non-spinning staff attacks deal 5 damage per hit.
- The staff can be used while regular webs are disabled.

