## Enemy Perception and Stealth

- A full stealth system has been added.
- Spider-Sense uses directional 3D audio to indicate where detection is coming from.
- Enemy awareness is displayed through a gradient directly over the character.
- Enemy markers use distance-scaled beacons.
- Enemy types are identified through clothing colors.
- Enemy health is communicated through equipment lights and visible body damage.
- Enemy outlines are hidden after the enemy becomes fully aware of the player.
- Enemy hearing is based on the player’s actual footstep audio.
- Moving slowly or remaining airborne allows hearing detection to decay.
- Enemies can still hear the player while cloaked.
- An unprepared stealth target begins calling for backup.
- Defeating the target before the call prevents reinforcements.
- Overshielded enemies must be struck from behind and cannot be webbed normally, except for the legs or head.
- Unaware enemies can be instantly knocked out by attacks from behind.
- Ground Pound attacks immediately reveal the player to nearby enemies.
- Enemies can be webbed in the face to prevent them from calling for help.

