## Combat Reactions and Damage Rules

- Light attacks trigger directional hit reactions instead of immediately throwing enemies into ragdoll.
- Reactions include face, side, body, and gut-hit animations.
- Stronger attacks and impacts can transition enemies into ragdoll.
- Ragdolled enemies can continue taking damage.
- Enemies can be killed while wrapped, although wrapped targets receive reduced damage.
- Unconscious enemies receive reduced incoming damage.
- A lethal attack against a conscious enemy first places them into a concussed state.
- Additional damage after concussion can defeat the enemy.
- The instant-kill impact threshold is 60 meters per second.
- Regular web shots require sustained webbing to fully wrap an enemy.
- Explosions can throw back every enemy class, including shielded targets.
- Player damage, including PvP damage, temporarily reduces movement speed.
- Players cannot manually respawn while injured or while enemies are actively aware of them.
- Low health is communicated through screen effects and warning audio.

