## Riot Shields and Overshields

- Riot shields primarily protect the torso and arms.
- Riot enemies can be attacked from behind or targeted at the feet.
- Webbing the front of a riot shield shocks the player through the tether.
- Overshielded enemies can appear among regular enemy groups.
- Overshielded enemies resist frontal web attacks unless they have been ragdolled.
- Webbing an overshielded enemy’s chest can shock the player.

