## Threat Level and Difficulty

- Threat Level ranges from -100 to +100.
- Negative Threat Level makes enemies increasingly deadly.
- Positive Threat Level makes enemies increasingly perceptive.
- Threat Level gradually moves back toward zero every five minutes.
- Combat difficulty also scales with the number of enemies defeated during the current run.
- Difficulty can scale through as many as 10 zone defeats.
- Higher difficulty increases enemy accuracy, damage, perception, and encounter pressure.
- Being defeated resets the current combat difficulty progression, but Threat Level does not reset.
- The scoreboard displays the player’s current Threat Level and total enemy defeats.

