## Crosshairs, Aiming, and Combat Feedback

- A completely new crosshair system has been added.
- Crosshairs use clear targeting feedback.
- Left- and right-hand crosshairs merge when targeting the same point.
- Portal aiming uses specialized crosshair behavior.
- Crosshairs compensate for VR hand jitter when held still.
- Asymmetrical crosshairs improve visibility at longer distances.
- Aim assist supports NPCs, portals, throwables, rockets, grenades, other players, and environmental objects.
- Targets can be switched easily during combat.
- Ballistic trajectory indicators assist with throwing objects.
- Crosshairs can be disabled.
- Aim-assist strength can be reduced to a near-disabled level.
- Enemy punch impacts use dedicated visual effects.
- NPC health, awareness, type, and distance information are integrated into the enemies themselves rather than relying entirely on floating UI.

