## Weather, Audio, and Immersion

- Motion-compensated weather has been added.
- Rain and storm effects remain positioned correctly around a moving player.
- Rain stops while the player is beneath cover and resumes after they return outside.
- Storms include expanded atmosphere, particles, and audio.
- Slow motion affects weather, impact sounds, car horns, particles, and environmental audio.
- A texture-noise system improves visibility and depth on flat rooftops and climbing surfaces.
- Dynamic custom footsteps have been added.
- Footstep pitch changes with avatar height and player speed.
- Players can select from shoes, bare feet, gear, heavy boots, heels, and robotic footsteps.

